WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.920
There's always been something a little off
about Thanos and his quest for galactic domination,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.820
and it has nothing to do with how much he
likes sitting down.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.600
It's all about the Infinity Gauntlet, the
artifact that Thanos will apparently wield

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.440
in Avengers: Infinity War, and the strange
fact that there seems to be more than one

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.440
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.380
"I only ask that you take this matter seriously."

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.140
We first got a glimpse of the Infinity Gauntlet,
which is specifically constructed to hold

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:34.460
the powerful Infinity Stones, in the background
of Odin's trophy room in 2011's Thor.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.720
In that scene, the gauntlet held the Infinity
Stones and was made for a right hand, which

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.260
is a subtly significant detail.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.820
The next time we saw the Gauntlet was during
a mid-credits scene after 2015's Avengers:

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:47.680
Age of Ultron.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.380
Thanos reached into a vault, put on a glove
with no stones on it and held it up.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.880
It looked to be on the left hand this time.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.040
"Illusion?"

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.680
"No, this is real."

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.620
But questions still lingered about his possession
of the artifact, like how could Thanos get

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.040
the Gauntlet when it's supposed to be safely
stowed away on Asgard?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.540
And aren't the Infinity Stones supposed to
be scattered around the universe anyway?

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.320
Two years ago, Marvel's Kevin Feige told CinemaBlend
there's a simple explanation, saying,

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.400
"There are two different gloves.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.340
That was not Odin's vault that you see at
the end [of Age of Ultron]."

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:22.700
"Alright!"

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.620
That sounds simple enough, but not everyone
read that interview, and besides, Marvel's

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.060
not always known for being so forthright.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:36.280
However, Thor: Ragnarok has now proven that,
indeed, Feige was telling the truth.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.960
In the film, we see Hela storm Odin's castle
and walk around his trophy room to reveal

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.260
that lots of the trophies are actually fake,
including the first-seen Infinity Gauntlet,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.620
which she unceremoniously knocks over.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.620
Soooo, that solves that.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.840
Now the stage is set for Infinity War, and
Feige's backstory checks out.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.680
There are two gloves, Thanos has one of them,
and he might just make good on that promise

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.500
after all.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.300
"And I will bathe star ways in your blood."

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:08.979
Now we just have to wait to find out if Thanos
has got the real deal and whether and how

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:13.599
he'll put his Infinity Gauntlet to use when
the Avengers: Infinity War hits theaters on

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.620
April 25th, 2018.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.340
"I'm gonna miss these little talks of ours."

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.680
Thanks for watching!

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.300
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.900
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

